{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Phinehas son of Eleazar</b> – The Holy One, blessed be He, made known to Moses that He would pay a good reward to Phinehas for his zealotry, which he was zealous for his Elohim, and for the vindication he wrought for Israel, to make atonement for them so that they did not all die in the plague. And He commanded him to make known to Israel that he is a priest forever, and this is the meaning of \"Therefore say\" — that he should announce this in Israel. Now the verse did not say \"and it shall be for him and for his seed after him a priesthood forever\" as it said of Aaron (Exodus 29:9), but rather it said \"a covenant of priesthood forever\" and it said \"My covenant of peace\" — that He would give him a covenant with peace joined to it, whereas of Aaron it is said \"for honor and for glory\" (Exodus 28:2). And therefore it said \"who was zealous for his Elohim,\" and the enlightened will understand. And it mentioned \"and the name of the Israelite man who was slain\" and \"and the name of the woman who was slain,\" to make known that he was worthy of this great reward, for he killed a prince in Israel and a daughter of a king of the nations and did not fear them in his zealotry for his Elohim. And after He gave his good reward to the righteous one, He commanded him to exact retribution from the wicked and said to him, \"Harass the Midianites,\" and He commanded him to take a census of the people first. And this is the meaning of \"And it came to pass after the plague\" (Numbers 26:1), for the census would come first:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:38.711857093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}